# UNERA V2 — Check icon (success-hero stroked check)

**Product flows** under `NewUnera/` use a **single stroked check** that matches the inner SVG of `.success-icon-animated` (see `.cursor/rules/newunera-success-screen-hero.mdc`). It is **not** the Material Symbols filled `check` in `0 -960 960 960` space — that variant is not used for steppers and flow chips in the current system.

- **Path:** `M5 13l4 4L19 7` in `viewBox="0 0 24 24"`.
- **Render:** `fill="none"`, `stroke="currentColor"`, `stroke-width="3"`, `stroke-linecap="round"`, `stroke-linejoin="round"`.
- **Class:** `unera-checkmark` on the `<svg>` for sizing hooks.

Parent surfaces (e.g. `.step.completed .step-circle`, `.success-icon-animated`, `.ts-icon.ts-check`, `.proc-icon.done`, `.notification-icon`) set **`color: var(--brand-white)`** (or an appropriate token) so `currentColor` matches the surface — not a hardcoded `stroke="white"` in markup where avoidable.

## Canonical markup

```html
<svg class="unera-checkmark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
  <path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
</svg>
```

## Required CSS (stroke — `fill: none`, not filled path)

```css
.unera-checkmark {
  display: block;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  fill: none;
}
```

Size with context rules, e.g.:

- `.step.completed .step-circle .unera-checkmark` → typically `22px` × `22px`
- `.success-icon-animated > .unera-checkmark` → typically `56px` × `56px` (100px circle hero)

## JS constant (dynamic stepper, trackers, proc rows)

```js
const UNERA_CHECKMARK_SVG = '<svg class="unera-checkmark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>';
```

Use `innerHTML = UNERA_CHECKMARK_SVG` for completed states; use `textContent = String(n)` for step numbers (clears SVG).

## Where this applies (`NewUnera/`)

| Surface | Selector / context |
|--------|---------------------|
| Desktop stepper | `#dynamicStepper .step.completed .step-circle` |
| Success hero | `.success-icon-animated` inner check (and `-lg` variants) |
| Redeem tx tracker | `.ts-icon.ts-check` |
| Get processing list | `.proc-icon.done` |
| Stake / notification | `.notification-icon .unera-checkmark`, `.token-check` (selected) |

**Reference implementations:** `NewUnera/add-money.html`, `NewUnera/exchange.html`, `NewUnera/get-unera-cad.html`, `NewUnera/redeem-unera-cad.html`, `NewUnera/send-enhanced.html`, `NewUnera/stake.html`.

## Do not

- Do **not** replace this stroked mark with a **filled** polyline/legacy single-path `fill: currentColor` on the `M5 13l4` segment — that reads as a different weight than the success hero.
- Do **not** use Unicode `✓` inside `.step-circle`, `.ts-icon.ts-check`, or `.proc-icon.done` for the primary check affordance.
- For **other** UI (unrelated icon buttons), use Material Symbols per `.cursor/rules/newunera-icons.mdc` — do not conflate that system with the **flow** `unera-checkmark` above.

## Out of scope

- **Copy-only** labels (e.g. "✓ Verified", "Completed ✓") may stay as text.
- **Pseudo-elements** with `content: '✓'` need a different pattern if they must match this icon (real element or background SVG).
